TidaLunar - Linux .tar.gz package
==================================

Quick start:
  tar -xzf tidalunar-<version>-linux-<arch>.tar.gz
  cd tidalunar-<version>-linux-<arch>/
  ./tidalunar

Sandbox status
==============
This .tar.gz package does NOT install the Chromium sandbox helper.
Depending on your distro, TidaLunar will run with one of:

  * Namespace sandbox (Debian 12+, Fedora 39+, Arch, openSUSE Leap 15.5+,
    Linux Mint 22, Ubuntu 22.04) -- sandboxing active.
  * Seccomp-only or no sandbox (Ubuntu 24.04+ with default kernel
    hardening, or kernels without unprivileged user namespaces) --
    reduced sandboxing.

If you want the full Chromium sandbox on Ubuntu 24.04+, install the .deb
package instead:

  sudo dpkg -i tidalunar_<version>_<arch>.deb

The .deb ships a setuid sandbox helper, an AppArmor profile, and a
runtime probe that picks the right sandbox mode at install time.

Updates
=======
TidaLunar self-updates silently into a copy under
~/.local/share/tidalunar/. The .tar.gz file you ran is only used for
the initial install; you can delete it after first launch.
